  "problem": "The number of roses and orchids in Margaret's garden is shown in the following table:\n\n| Roses | Orchids |\n| --- | --- |\n| $33$ | $18$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIn Serena's garden, there are approximately $30$ orchids. The ratio of the number of roses to the number of orchids is equal in both gardens. By rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the number of roses in Serena's garden.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's round the number of roses and orchids in Margaret's garden:\n\n- Roses: $33⟶30$\n\n- Orchids: $18⟶20$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of roses to the number of orchids (expressed as a fraction) is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{30}{20}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the number of roses and the denominator represents the number of orchids.\n\nDividing the numerator and denominator by $10$ gives an equivalent fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{30÷10}{20÷10}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $30$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $15$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 15}{2\\times 15}=\\frac{45}{30}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are approximately $45$ roses in Serena's garden.",
